# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# Start the server first (npm start, after copying .env.example to .env), then click Send Request above any request.
# A browser sends the Origin header by itself; here you send it by hand, to see what the API answers each page.

### The roasts, with helmet's headers and no X-Powered-By: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/roasts

### From the club's web page: 200 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://www.beanthere.example
GET http://localhost:3100/roasts
Origin: https://www.beanthere.example

### From another site's page: 200, but no Access-Control-Allow-Origin, so a browser hides the answer
GET http://localhost:3100/roasts
Origin: https://coffee-deals.example

### A preflight, as a browser sends it before a PATCH with a token: 204, allowing PATCH
OPTIONS http://localhost:3100/members/me
Origin: https://www.beanthere.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: PATCH
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

### Dana signs in: 200 with a token (the requests below use it)
# @name signIn
POST http://localhost:3100/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "dana@beanthere.example", "password": "dana-test-password" }

### Dana's own record: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/members/me
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}

### A change that tries to make Dana an admin: 200, but only favoriteRoast changes
PATCH http://localhost:3100/members/me
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "favoriteRoast": "Night Owl", "role": "admin", "cupsLeft": 999 }

### An operator object instead of an email: 400
POST http://localhost:3100/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": { "$gt": "" }, "password": "dana-test-password" }

### A wrong password: 401. Send it again until the answer is 429 (the sign-ins above count as tries too)
POST http://localhost:3100/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "dana@beanthere.example", "password": "a-wrong-guess" }
